IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc3-forfeiture.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II.1 Terrorism, "Seizure and Restraint of Property" (s 83.13) and "Forfeiture of Property" (ss 83.14 to 83.17).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), written by part agent ccc3 from the text alone. The text is a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
--
-- WHO THIS IS ABOUT. The Attorney General applies, a judge of the Federal Court decides, a manager is appointed. It is encoded for what it means to the person whose property is
-- seized, restrained or forfeited, who may be named, notified and heard, and by when they must move. There is no seat for an official (the brief).
--
-- READING A RESULT (rule of 2026-10-29 and the ruling of 2026-11-12): as in `ccc3-interpretation.l4`. A power ("may") with an "if" gate answers NOTHING when the gate fails (tag GATE-A);
-- a "may" function gated by "where", "when", "upon" or a stated period answers JUST FALSE as the 2026-11-05 rulings say, and is listed for a lawyer (tag GATE-B); a "shall" duty whose "if" or "where" is unmet
-- answers JUST FALSE (the duty does not arise; fork F-ccc3-6); the functions named for being "entitled" are a separate group for a lawyer (tag ENTITLED). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Provisions that apply sections of Part XII.2 (ss 462.32 to 462.46) and of Part XV to the warrants and orders made here are encoded as tables of the provisions they apply. The seam PLAN.md lists
-- from sections 83.13 and 83.14 into ccc14 (`s 462.34 the review ... has been applied for`) is not taken: no sentence of this part turns on that answer (NOTES.md, Seams).

§ `Section 83.13 -- Seizure and restraint of assets`

-- (1) "Where a judge of the Federal Court, on an ex parte application by the Attorney General, after examining the application in private, is satisfied ... the judge may issue (a) ... a warrant ...; or (b) ... a restraint order".
-- GATE-B: "Where" is the gate of the whole grant, so when it fails the answer is JUST FALSE (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05); GATE-A: "(a) if the property is situated in Canada".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-11,F-ccc3-20 | s 83.13(1) the judge may issue the warrant or restraint order | s 83.13(1)*
-- src:1554 | Seizure and restraint of assets
-- src:1555 | 83.13 (1) Where a judge of the Federal Court, on an ex parte application by the Attorney General, after examining the application in private, is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in any building, receptacle or place any property in respect of which an order of forfeiture may be made under subsection 83.14(5), the judge may issue
-- src:1556 | (a) if the property is situated in Canada, a warrant authorizing a person named therein or a peace officer to search the building, receptacle or place for that property and to seize that property and any other property in respect of which that person or peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, that an order of forfeiture may be made under that subsection; or
-- src:1557 | (b) if the property is situated in or outside Canada, a restraint order prohibiting any person from disposing of, or otherwise dealing with any interest in, that property other than as may be specified in the order.
@ref s 83.13(1) (src:1554-1557)
DECLARE `s 83.13(1) order` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.13(1)(a) a warrant authorizing a person named in it or a peace officer to search the building, receptacle or place for the property and to seize it`
    `s 83.13(1)(b) a restraint order prohibiting any person from disposing of, or otherwise dealing with any interest in, the property`

@ref s 83.13(1) (src:1554-1557)
GIVEN `the judge is a judge of the Federal Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is an ex parte application by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge has examined the application in private` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in any building, receptacle or place any property in respect of which an order of forfeiture may be made under subsection 83.14(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order` IS A `s 83.13(1) order`
      `the property is situated in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.13(1) the judge may issue the warrant or restraint order` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `the judge is a judge of the Federal Court`
            AND `the application is an ex parte application by the Attorney General`
            AND `the judge has examined the application in private`
            AND `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in any building, receptacle or place any property in respect of which an order of forfeiture may be made under subsection 83.14(5)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a judge of the Federal Court, on an ex parte application by the Attorney General, after examining the application in private, is satisfied"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the order`
         WHEN `s 83.13(1)(a) a warrant authorizing a person named in it or a peace officer to search the building, receptacle or place for the property and to seize it` THEN
             IF `the property is situated in Canada`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the property is situated in Canada, a warrant"
         WHEN `s 83.13(1)(b) a restraint order prohibiting any person from disposing of, or otherwise dealing with any interest in, the property` THEN JUST TRUE

-- (1.1) the affidavit and the adverse inference. "no adverse inference shall be drawn" is a flat negative, answered as the bar.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.13(1.1) the affidavit may be sworn on information and belief; s 83.13(1.1) no adverse inference is to be drawn from the failure | s 83.13(1.1)
-- src:1558 | Contents of application
-- src:1559 | (1.1) An affidavit in support of an application under subsection (1) may be sworn on information and belief, and, notwithstanding the Federal Court Rules, 1998, no adverse inference shall be drawn from a failure to provide evidence of persons having personal knowledge of material facts.
@ref s 83.13(1.1) (src:1558-1559)
GIVEN `the affidavit is in support of an application under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.13(1.1) the affidavit may be sworn on information and belief` MEANS
    IF `the affidavit is in support of an application under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An affidavit in support of an application under subsection (1) may be sworn on information and belief"

@ref s 83.13(1.1) (src:1558-1559)
GIVEN `the application is under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is a failure to provide evidence of persons having personal knowledge of material facts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.13(1.1) no adverse inference is to be drawn from the failure` MEANS
    IF `the application is under subsection (1)` AND `the failure is a failure to provide evidence of persons having personal knowledge of material facts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no adverse inference shall be drawn from a failure to provide evidence of persons having personal knowledge of material facts"

-- (2) "On an application under subsection (1), at the request of the Attorney General, if a judge is of the opinion that the circumstances so require, the judge may (a) appoint ...; and (b) require any person having possession ...".
-- GATE-B (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, group (i), fork F-ccc3-11): "On an application under subsection (1), at the request of the Attorney General" gates the whole power: JUST FALSE without them.
-- GATE-A: "if a judge is of the opinion that the circumstances so require": NOTHING when it fails (fork F-ccc3-20).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-11,F-ccc3-20 | s 83.13(2) the judge may appoint a person to manage the property and require possession to be given | s 83.13(2)*
-- src:1560 | Appointment of manager
-- src:1561 | (2) On an application under subsection (1), at the request of the Attorney General, if a judge is of the opinion that the circumstances so require, the judge may
-- src:1562 | (a) appoint a person to take control of, and to manage or otherwise deal with, all or part of the property in accordance with the directions of the judge; and
-- src:1563 | (b) require any person having possession of that property to give possession of the property to the person appointed under paragraph (a).
@ref s 83.13(2) (src:1560-1563)
GIVEN `the request is made on an application under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that the circumstances so require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.13(2) the judge may appoint a person to manage the property and require possession to be given` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the request is made on an application under subsection (1)` AND `the request is made by the Attorney General`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On an application under subsection (1), at the request of the Attorney General"
    ELSE IF `the judge is of the opinion that the circumstances so require`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a judge is of the opinion that the circumstances so require, the judge may"

-- (3) "When the Attorney General of Canada so requests, a judge appointing a person under subsection (2) shall appoint the Minister of Public Works and Government Services."
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6 | s 83.13(3) the judge must appoint the Minister of Public Works and Government Services | s 83.13(3)
-- src:1564 | Appointment of Minister of Public Works and Government Services
-- src:1565 | (3) When the Attorney General of Canada so requests, a judge appointing a person under subsection (2) shall appoint the Minister of Public Works and Government Services.
@ref s 83.13(3) (src:1564-1565)
GIVEN `the Attorney General of Canada so requests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge appoints a person under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.13(3) the judge must appoint the Minister of Public Works and Government Services` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General of Canada so requests` AND `the judge appoints a person under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the Attorney General of Canada so requests, a judge appointing a person under subsection (2) shall appoint"

-- (4) The power to manage "includes" three powers: the list is open. (c) is "other than real property or a conveyance".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-9 | s 83.13(4) the power to manage includes the power | s 83.13(4)*
-- src:1566 | Power to manage
-- src:1567 | (4) The power to manage or otherwise deal with property under subsection (2) includes
-- src:1568 | (a) the power to make an interlocutory sale of perishable or rapidly depreciating property;
-- src:1569 | (b) the power to destroy, in accordance with subsections (5) to (8), property that has little or no value; and
-- src:1570 | (c) the power to have property, other than real property or a conveyance, forfeited to Her Majesty in accordance with subsection (8.1).
@ref s 83.13(4) (src:1566-1570)
DECLARE `s 83.13(4) power` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.13(4)(a) the power to make an interlocutory sale of perishable or rapidly depreciating property`
    `s 83.13(4)(b) the power to destroy, in accordance with subsections (5) to (8), property that has little or no value`
    `s 83.13(4)(c) the power to have property forfeited to Her Majesty in accordance with subsection (8.1)`
    `s 83.13(4) another power`

@ref s 83.13(4) (src:1566-1570)
GIVEN power IS A `s 83.13(4) power`
      `the property is real property or a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.13(4) the power to manage includes the power` MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    WHEN `s 83.13(4)(a) the power to make an interlocutory sale of perishable or rapidly depreciating property` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.13(4)(b) the power to destroy, in accordance with subsections (5) to (8), property that has little or no value` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.13(4)(c) the power to have property forfeited to Her Majesty in accordance with subsection (8.1)` THEN
        IF `the property is real property or a conveyance`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the power to have property, other than real property or a conveyance, forfeited to Her Majesty"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.13(4) another power` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes"

