-- (8.1) The notice must specify "a period of 60 days" (read as exactly 60: fork F-ccc3-12); no one may make an application asserting an interest "during that period".
-- The period is taken as 60 days beginning on the day the notice is given or published (first day to first day + 59).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6,F-ccc3-9,F-ccc3-12 | s 83.13(8.1) the judge must order the property forfeited to Her Majesty | s 83.13(8.1)*
-- src:1581 | Forfeiture order
-- src:1582 | (8.1) On application by a person who is appointed to manage the property, a judge of the Federal Court shall order that the property, other than real property or a conveyance, be forfeited to Her Majesty to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law if
-- src:1583 | (a) a notice is given or published in the manner that the judge directs or that may be specified in the rules of the Federal Court;
-- src:1584 | (b) the notice specifies a period of 60 days during which a person may make an application to the judge asserting their interest in the property; and
-- src:1585 | (c) during that period, no one makes such an application.
@ref s 83.13(8.1) (src:1581-1585)
GIVEN `the application is made by the person appointed to manage the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is real property or a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice is given or published in the manner that the judge directs or that may be specified in the rules of the Federal Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days of the period the notice specifies` IS A NUMBER
      `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the day on which a person made an application asserting an interest in the property, if one did` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.13(8.1) the judge must order the property forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application is made by the person appointed to manage the property`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application by a person who is appointed to manage the property"
    ELSE IF `the property is real property or a conveyance`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than real property or a conveyance"
         ELSE IF     `a notice is given or published in the manner that the judge directs or that may be specified in the rules of the Federal Court`
                 AND `the number of days of the period the notice specifies` EQUALS 60
                 AND `no one makes such an application during that period`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) a notice is given or published in the manner that the judge directs"
    WHERE
        `no one makes such an application during that period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which a person made an application asserting an interest in the property, if one did`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST asserted THEN NOT (asserted AT LEAST `the first day of the period` AND asserted AT MOST (`the first day of the period` PLUS 59))

