-- (11) and (12): provisions applied, with the modifications the circumstances require, to a warrant under (1)(a) and to an order under (1)(b). The section numbers are decimals (462.34 to 462.35 takes in 462.341 and the like).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-15 | s 83.13(11) the provision applies to a warrant issued under paragraph (1)(a); s 83.13(11) the peace officer may execute the warrant | s 83.13(11)
-- src:1592 | Procedure
-- src:1593 | (11) Subsection 462.32(4), sections 462.34 to 462.35 and 462.4, subsection 487(3) and section 488 apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to a warrant issued under paragraph (1)(a). Any peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed.
@ref s 83.13(11) (src:1592-1593)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the warrant was issued under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.13(11) the provision applies to a warrant issued under paragraph (1)(a)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the warrant was issued under paragraph (1)(a)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to a warrant issued under paragraph (1)(a)"
    ELSE IF     (provision's `section` EQUALS 462.32 AND provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(4)")
            OR (provision's `section` AT LEAST 462.34 AND provision's `section` AT MOST 462.35)
            OR provision's `section` EQUALS 462.4
            OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 487 AND provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(3)")
            OR provision's `section` EQUALS 488
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Subsection 462.32(4), sections 462.34 to 462.35 and 462.4, subsection 487(3) and section 488 apply"

@ref s 83.13(11) (src:1592-1593)
GIVEN `the peace officer has authority to act as a peace officer in the place where the warrant is executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.13(11) the peace officer may execute the warrant` MEANS
    IF `the peace officer has authority to act as a peace officer in the place where the warrant is executed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed"

-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-15 | s 83.13(12) the provision applies to an order issued under paragraph (1)(b) | s 83.13(12)
